# A rank-one density certificate for the binary twenty-space

The first 54 matrices are words in the two action matrices. Seven powers of the
seven-cycle give P = 1 + B + ... + B⁶. The product P(A + word₁₄)P is rank one.
Twenty left translates and twenty right translates span its full column and row
spaces. Their checked linear combinations give the rank-one matrices eᵢ vᵀ and
u eⱼᵀ, whose products are matrix units because vᵀu = 1.

The table indices are: 0–53 for words, 54–60 for the powers of B,
61 for P, 62 for A + word₁₄, 63 for their product, and 64 for R.
Indices 65–84 and 85–104 are the left and right translates of R;
105–124 and 125–144 are the resulting column and row matrices.

All stored calculations below are checked by kernel reduction of natural-number
XOR and bit operations, using the soundness theorem for binary row multiplication.
Source: the candidate used in Aschbacher–Smith K.1.2, p.452/PDF p.463.
-/

